<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">OGPU</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Joint State Political Directorate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The OGPU (Joint State Political Directorate) was the Soviet political police from 1923 to 1934, successor to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheka">Cheka</a> and GPU. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky">Felix Dzerzhinsky</a> and then Vyacheslav Menzhinsky, it suppressed opposition, staged early show trials and enforced the collectivisation of agriculture, deporting some two million peasants as kulaks to special settlements and expanding the system of forced-labour camps. In 1934 it was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ogpu.jpg" alt="OGPU" width="176" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GPU_15th_anniversary_emblem.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
